GL Code & Cost Code Prediction System - Technical Documentation
Use Case: Automated GL Code and Cost Code Tagging for Non-PO Invoice Approval

1. Executive Summary
1.1 Business Problem
In enterprise procurement and accounts payable operations, invoices that lack a Purchase Order (PO) reference present a unique challenge. Approvers need to:

Assign appropriate General Ledger (GL) Codes for proper financial classification
Assign Cost Centre (CC) Codes for budget allocation
Make decisions quickly without slowing down the approval workflow
Maintain consistency in coding decisions across similar invoices
Manual assignment is time-consuming, error-prone, and lacks the ability to leverage historical patterns effectively. This leads to inconsistent coding, delayed approvals, and potential compliance issues.

1.2 Solution Overview
The GL Code & Cost Code Prediction System is an AI-powered Azure Function that automatically analyzes invoice line items and predicts the most appropriate GL Code and Cost Centre based on historical data and LLM-based reasoning.

Technique	Purpose
Azure AI Search (Vector Search)	Retrieves semantically similar historical line descriptions
LLM-Based GL Category Identification	Uses Azure OpenAI to identify relevant GL categories for new line descriptions
LLM-Based Line Description Matching	Matches ambiguous lines to the most relevant historical line description
Frequency & Recency Algorithm	Calculates confidence scores based on historical usage patterns
Parallel Processing	Processes multiple line items concurrently for performance
1.3 Key Capabilities
Multi-Stage LLM Pipeline: Two-stage LLM processing for category identification and line matching
Historical Data Analysis: Leverages past invoice coding decisions via Azure AI Search
Confidence Scoring: Provides confidence percentages using frequency, recency, and semantic similarity scores
Approver-Aware CC Prediction: Filters Cost Centre predictions based on the current approver's historical coding patterns
Parallel Processing: Uses ThreadPoolExecutor for concurrent line item processing
Dynamic Configuration: All field mappings, prompts, and parameters are configurable via Azure Blob Storage
Master Data Integration: Supports GL category master data with explanations
Low Confidence Detection: Flags predictions based on newly created GL categories
